# Discussion

<Interpret. Lead with what reproduced and why it is robust (scale/seed-invariant, across
several read-outs). Then any negative result: state the mechanism/cause and its downstream
consequences (often one modelling fact explains several panel mismatches — say so rather
than listing them as independent failures). Then the reproduction-vs-replication framing
(below) and the accepted limitations.>

**Reproduction vs. replication.** In the NASEM (2019) terminology, *reproduction* re-runs
the same code on the same data; *replication* re-derives a paper's findings with
**independent methods and independently-sourced data** — which is what this is. Separate
**mechanism-level** targets (a sign / pattern / ordering that any reasonable input
reproduces) from **decimal-level** targets (a number needing the paper's exact input): the
former reproduce; the latter are capped by unavailable inputs and stated as limitations,
never claimed as matches.

## Replication scorecard

